---
import ToolLayout from '../../layouts/ToolLayout.astro';
import MarginMarkupCalculator from '../../components/MarginMarkupCalculator.jsx';
---
<ToolLayout title="Profit Margin vs Markup Calculator" description="See both margin and markup percentage from the same cost and selling price — they're not the same number.">
  <MarginMarkupCalculator client:load slot="tool" />
  <h2>Why people mix these up</h2>
  <p>A 50% markup on a $40 cost gives a $60 price — but that's only a 33% margin, not 50%. Pricing based on the wrong one is a common way businesses under-price their product.</p>

  <h2>Common mistakes</h2>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Setting a target margin but calculating it as markup</strong> (or vice versa), resulting in a different profit than intended.</li>
    <li><strong>Not recalculating when costs change</strong>, letting margin quietly erode over time even though the markup percentage stayed the same.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Use cases</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>Setting a selling price that achieves a specific target margin</li>
    <li>Understanding the real margin behind a chosen markup percentage</li>
    <li>Auditing pricing to ensure margins haven't eroded as costs changed</li>
  </ul>
</ToolLayout>
